          "kind": "finished",
          "message": "## Done — a real INI parser, not a fixture table\n\n`moon test` passes **105/105** tests from a clean rebuild (`moon clean` → `moon test`), including the 12 provided public cases (two of them property-based) and 93 cases of my own derived from `specs/ini.md`.\n\n### Structure (root package, one concern per file)\n\n| file | role |\n| --- | --- |\n| [ini_error.mbt](D:/a/openseek-swe-agi/openseek-swe-agi/tasks/ini_run_1/ini_error.mbt) | `ParseError(line, message)` suberror |\n| [ini_scan.mbt](D:/a/openseek-swe-agi/openseek-swe-agi/tasks/ini_run_1/ini_scan.mbt) | char classes, LF/CRLF line splitting, blank trimming, inline-comment cutting, separator lookup, trailing-backslash accounting |\n| [ini_value.mbt](D:/a/openseek-swe-agi/openseek-swe-agi/tasks/ini_run_1/ini_value.mbt) | the three carriers (unquoted / `\"…\"` / `'…'`), quoted scanning, continuation joining, per-carrier escape decoding |\n| [ini_structure.mbt](D:/a/openseek-swe-agi/openseek-swe-agi/tasks/ini_run_1/ini_structure.mbt) | section-name extraction/quoting rules, key validation |\n| [ini_parser.mbt](D:/a/openseek-swe-agi/openseek-swe-agi/tasks/ini_run_1/ini_parser.mbt) | `parse`: single left-to-right pass, section re-open, last-wins |\n| [ini_printer.mbt](D:/a/openseek-swe-agi/openseek-swe-agi/tasks/ini_run_1/ini_printer.mbt) | `print`: always double-quoted values, careful section names |\n\nTests: [ini_edge_test.mbt](D:/a/openseek-swe-agi/openseek-swe-agi/tasks/ini_run_1/ini_edge_test.mbt) (spec-section groups: lines, comments, sections, entries, quoted values/escapes, the N=1..4 continuation table, all required rejections, printing), [ini_realworld_test.mbt](D:/a/openseek-swe-agi/openseek-swe-agi/tasks/ini_run_1/ini_realworld_test.mbt) (git config, systemd unit, php.ini, Windows paths), plus a 1000-case round-trip and a 500-case never-panic property run. Documentation: [README.md](D:/a/openseek-swe-agi/openseek-swe-agi/tasks/ini_run_1/README.md).\n\n### Key implementation points\n\n- **Char-indexed scanning.** The input is read once into `Array[Char]`; each line is an `ArrayView[Char]`. This fixed a real bug found by the round-trip property: `StringView` indices are UTF-16 code units, so an emoji put a surrogate half in the middle of a structural scan. Nothing copies except owned keys and joined values.\n- **Continuation decided before escapes** by counting the raw trailing-backslash run (odd → marker, even → escaped literals), then joining the next line verbatim and decoding once — matching the spec's N=1..4 table.\n- **Carrier-specific escapes** (`\\\\ \\n \\r \\t` unquoted; plus `\\\"` in `\"…\"`; only `\\\\` and `\\'` in `'…'`), unknown sequences keeping the backslash so `C:\\Program Files` is itself.\n- **Line-based section recognition**, so `key=value [section]` stays one entry; strict headers (`[a]b`, `[[nested]]`, `[]`, `[a] trailing` all rejected).\n- **`print` is total for unrestricted values** (double quotes with `\\\\ \\\" \\n \\r \\t` escapes) and quotes a section name only when the parser would otherwise change it — blank-padded names *and* names that start and end with the same quote character.\n\n### Verification and the audit\n\nAn independent audit (`@builtin/review.mbtx`) swept 1555 header texts and 7381 value texts and confirmed every required rejection fires and no valid form is over-rejected. It found one genuine contract violation, which I fixed: `print` emitted a name like `\"\"` bare, and the parser stripped its quote pair on the way back — such names are now wrapped in one more pair (`[\"\"\"\"]` → `\"\"`), with tests. I also made the CR rule exact (a CR is content unless it is the CR of a CRLF; previously a CR at end of input was silently dropped, contradicting the README) and documented both choices.\n\n`moon check` reports **0 errors**; the only remaining warnings come from the files I was told not to modify (`ini_spec.mbt`'s deprecated `derive(...)`, `ini_qc.mbt`'s promoted impls, `moon.pkg`'s import); none originate in my code. I restored `ini_spec.mbt` and `ini_qc.mbt` byte-for-byte after `moon fmt` migrated their deprecated syntax (verified against `git show HEAD:tasks/ini/…`), and `moon.pkg` now declares `moonbitlang/core/test` as a `for \"test\"` import, which removes the pre-existing unused-import warning while keeping it available to black-box tests. `moon fmt` and `moon info` have been run; `pkg.generated.mbti` is refreshed.\n"
        }
