          "message": "All work is complete. Final verification: `moon check` reports 0 errors (the 6 remaining warnings all come from the three protected files), `moon test` passes 53/53, and `moon fmt --check` flags only the two protected files that ship unformatted.\n\n## What I built\n\nA real scan → parse → print pipeline in the root `ini` package (so `@ini.parse` / `@ini.print` stay where the tests call them):\n\n| File | Role |\n| --- | --- |\n| [scan.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_2\\scan.mbt) | physical lines (LF/CRLF), blank classification, trimming, character ranges, trailing-backslash runs |\n| [value.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_2\\value.mbt) | the three value carriers, quoted-value scanning, inline comments, per-carrier escape decoding |\n| [section.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_2\\section.mbt) | `[name]` headers, quote stripping, bracket validation |\n| [parser.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_2\\parser.mbt) | line dispatch, first-separator key/value split, continuations, document assembly |\n| [printer.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_2\\printer.mbt) | `print`, all values double-quoted, section names re-quoted when bare would not read back |\n| [ini_error.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_2\\ini_error.mbt) | `IniError.SyntaxError` with a message naming the physical line |\n| [ini_edge_test.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_2\\ini_edge_test.mbt) | 41 added tests derived from `specs/ini.md` |\n| [README.md](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_2\\README.md) | architecture, algorithms, usage, testing, design rationale |\n\nKey correctness decisions:\n\n- **Continuation is decided on raw text before escapes**: an odd trailing backslash run is a marker (removed, next line appended verbatim), an even run is escaped literals — reproducing the N=1..4 table, `k=a\\\\\\n`, and `path=C:\\Program Files\\` + `nextkey=value`.\n- **Per-carrier escape table**: unquoted/double decode `\\\\ \\n \\r \\t` (double also `\\\"`), single decodes only `\\\\ \\'`; everything else keeps its backslash so `C:\\Program` and `'a\\nb'` survive.\n- **Inline comments** need a blank before `;`/`#`, so `a;b` stays a value while `a ; b` is cut; quoted values disable comment scanning entirely.\n- **Duplicates/re-open** fall out of writing into the currently selected map, so last-wins and section re-opening need no special case.\n\nAn independent audit I ran flagged two genuine round-trip gaps, which are now fixed and covered by tests: `print` now re-quotes section names that are themselves quote-wrapped (`\"x\"` → `['\"x\"']`) or that carry surrounding blanks, and quoted names keep their interior padding (`[\"  padded  \"]` → `  padded  `, only the blanks outside the quote pair are trimmed).\n\nThe protected files (`ini_spec.mbt`, `ini_qc.mbt`, `ini_pub_test.mbt`, `specs/`) are byte-identical to what was provided — I reverted the cosmetic reformatting `moon fmt` applied to them and verified formatting of my own files with `moon fmt --check`."
