          "message": "Done. `moon test` is green (68/68) and `moon check` is clean.\n\n## What I built\n\nA real parser, not fixture matching — scanning → value parsing → assembly → printing, in focused files of the root `tonyfettes/ini` package:\n\n| file | role |\n| --- | --- |\n| [character.mbt](D:/a/openseek-swe-agi/openseek-swe-agi/tasks/ini_run_3/character.mbt) | `is_blank`/`is_control`, window trims over `Array[Char]` |\n| [source_lines.mbt](D:/a/openseek-swe-agi/openseek-swe-agi/tasks/ini_run_3/source_lines.mbt) | LF/CRLF splitting, BOM, no phantom line after a final line break |\n| [section.mbt](D:/a/openseek-swe-agi/openseek-swe-agi/tasks/ini_run_3/section.mbt) | `[name]`: bracket validation, wrapping-quote strip, blank-name rejection |\n| [entry.mbt](D:/a/openseek-swe-agi/openseek-swe-agi/tasks/ini_run_3/entry.mbt) | first `=`/`:` wins, key trimming and control-character check |\n| [value.mbt](D:/a/openseek-swe-agi/openseek-swe-agi/tasks/ini_run_3/value.mbt) | three carriers, per-carrier escape tables, inline comments, continuations |\n| [ini.mbt](D:/a/openseek-swe-agi/openseek-swe-agi/tasks/ini_run_3/ini.mbt) | line classification, section re-opening, document assembly |\n| [printer.mbt](D:/a/openseek-swe-agi/openseek-swe-agi/tasks/ini_run_3/printer.mbt) | `print` — every value double quoted, names wrapped only when needed |\n\nKey ordering decisions: carrier chosen by the first non-blank character; continuation decided on raw text *before* escapes (odd run = marker, even = literals); trimming before decoding so `k=a\\\\\\n` keeps its newline; inline comments stripped before a marker can be read, so a `\\` inside a comment can never swallow the next line.\n\nI also ran an independent audit against `specs/ini.md` and fixed every finding: a dangling marker at the end of a newline-terminated file now raises (`invalid/backslash-continuation-no-newline`), a marker inside an inline comment no longer eats the following entry, a lone trailing `\\r` stays content